     "page": 1,
     "text": "Wilcox PLC Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Douglas Reid in consultation on September 13, 2025. Mr. Reid was referred for evaluation and management of his HIV, which has been under treatment with antiretroviral therapy (ART) for 18.8 years. His viral load has been undetectable for 103 months, and his latest CD4 count stands at 769 cells/mm3. His current regimen includes darunavir-cobicistat 800/150 mg, which he has been taking without issues. His HIV remains well controlled, with no AIDS-defining illnesses or complications from hepatitis coinfection.\n\nDuring the visit, Mr. Reid’s blood pressure was 136/76 mmHg, and his weight was 207 pounds. His physical exam was otherwise unremarkable, with no acute distress noted. The remainder of the examination, including musculoskeletal, cardiovascular, and respiratory systems, was within normal limits. He also reported no new or worsening symptoms.\n\nSocial history reveals that Mr. Reid is a former smoker, having smoked cigarettes at a rate of 1.5 packs per day until he quit on March 24, 2022. He consumes alcohol at a rate of approximately three drinks per week.\n\nGiven the stability of his HIV status and the effective management with his current medication regimen, I recommend continuing darunavir-cobicistat 800/150 mg as prescribed. I also suggest ongoing monitoring of his viral load and CD4 count to ensure continued control of his HIV infection.\n\nThank you for this referral. Please feel free to reach out should any further consultations or adjustments in his care be needed.\n\nBest regards,\n\nDr. Autumn Robles\nRheumatologist\n"
    }
